# The Pour V4 captive slide; reviewed after the published STEP and print-surface payload matched.
# Findings read once from the current STL. Physical release, strength and lifetime remain unmeasured.

[ceiling] This is the single moving crossbar underside at Z3.56. Its two bed-rooted legs anchor the 13 mm span along Y; the native first crossbar layer contains 37 Y-directed bridge roads with both leg anchors. The fixed plinth stops at Z3.08, leaving the intended nominal 0.48 mm release air. The 3.36 mm bar carries the local sliding reference.
alternatives: A solid bridge down to the plinth would join the moving and fixed bodies. Slicer support under this crossbar would fill the deliberate release gap; the bar instead bridges its own two printed legs. Shortening the span would change the retained two-leg portal and its accessible finger opening.
